            "review_text": "rinimukherjee\nBangalore District, India183 contributions\n0\nUnlimited Buffet\nMay 2026 • Family\nTried Mr Môc Seafood Buffet in Da Nang and it’s definitely an experience.\nIf you’re a hardcore seafood lover, this place can feel like value for money. But if you’re vegetarian, this is not for you.\nIt’s a hands-on, slightly chaotic setup, you literally pick live seafood (crabs, prawns, etc.), bring it to your table, and cook it yourself in a hot pot or on the grill. Not for the faint-hearted… especially if you’re not used to your food “moving” before it’s cooked 😅\nThere are some meat options too, along with unlimited soft drinks and beer, which adds to the appeal.\nA quick tip: language can be a barrier, so keep a translator handy. Best way to navigate? Just observe what others are doing and follow along.\nOverall, less of a typical dining experience and more of a “dive in and figure it out” kind of place.\nRead more\nWritten May 7, 2026",
