            "review_title": "Review at Buffet Hải Sản Nha Trang Mr Mộc",
            "review_text": "eric s\n7 contributions\n0\na great seafood/hotpot buffet at a very fair price in Nha Trang\nDec 2024 • Solo\nLooking for an all you can eat seafood buffet at a very reasonable price? including free drinks, desserts, salads and more? Mr Moc has all of that and it is really good 👍🏻❤️😊\n\nThere are plenty of different options/items to choose from. Some live seashells and crabs even. Fish, meat and a few veggies (though I wish there would be more). Plenty of seashells. I mainly go there for oysters, big prawns and fresh seashells. At times they also have urchins.\n\nAs part of the dessert options very tasty (sweeeet) panna cotta. Some ice creams (vietnamese ;-).\n\nService is very \"enthusiastic\" as I see the words locals are using. Not highly professional but very kind and a great help the first time you are there. Not much English spoken but staff attending the tables (they will cook, grill for you if you are a \"beginner\" ;-). Staff at the reception have a good command of English. Price is just below 300K Dongs for adults. More than fair. No time pressure.\n\nBest is to avoid rush times after 6PM. 4 to 6 PM is usually super quiet and enjoyable.\n\nConvenient location and definitely a great option in my view. Food quality is good. At times better... at times a bit less but plenty of options to choose from. Bottom line: I really like that buffet and the great (very young) staff. Only negative: at times some of the staff (very few) interact with each another loudly and ... well...how to put that🤔... a bit in a childish way I would not expect in a restaurant... from the staff 😉 \nAlso some guests can be very loud. Especially big parties. Hence I tend to go from 3 to 6 PM as it is quiet 👍🏻😊\nRead more\nWritten December 20, 2024",
